.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-stream \- read a run line by line from standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
\fBkarvi\fR \fBstream\fR
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fB\-\fR
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" BEGIN GENERATED DESCRIPTION: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
.PP
Reads a run line by line from standard input and executes it as run would.
A line is skipped when blank or when its first character is ! or #. A line
beginning with \-\- is one run option: the word, then its value as the rest
of the line after a space or =, so \-\-target router1, \-\-target=router1,
\-\-tl "router1 router2", \-\-dispatch parallel, \-\-dp. Any other line is one
command, sent as written; \er at its end is read as \-\-cmd reads it, and a
line of \er alone sends a blank line. The targets and options stay from one
job to the next; the commands are the job's. A \-\-cmd, \-\-command, or \-\-cf
line is a command like a bare line, and \-\-expect, \-\-blind, and
\-\-blind\-return lines attach to the command before them. \-\-cf, \-\-tf, and
\-\-tfr may not name \-: standard input is the stream.
.SS "Directives, each a whole line"
.TP
\fB\-\-go\fR, \fB\-\-sendit\fR
Execute the draft as run; the targets and
options stay for the next job, the commands
clear; with no command to send, a notice
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\fR
Empty the commands; the targets and options
stay
.TP
\fB\-\-reset\fR
Empty the draft
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR, \fB\-\-quit\fR
Leave without executing; so do EOF (Ctrl\-D)
and Ctrl\-C
.PP
Typed at a terminal, a line is edited with Ctrl\-A, Ctrl\-E, Ctrl\-K, Ctrl\-U,
Ctrl\-W, and the arrows, and the up arrow recalls earlier lines. A line the
parser refuses is reported with its number and dropped. The exit is the
last executed job's, 0 when none ran; a read failure or a line over 1 MiB
ends the stream with stream_input_read_failed. Global options go before
the word: karvi \-\-quiet \-\-config FILE stream.
.SS "Options"
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-h\fR
Show this help
.\" END GENERATED DESCRIPTION
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi (1)
